Z||000000||Kwez||05-08-2001||06:40 PM||||hi again.<P>I currently have a 86 GT w. a 3speed auto.<P>I will eventually do an engine swap<BR>and<BR>want to convert to a manual transmisison<BR>and<BR>I will upgrade the suspension<BR>and<BR>I might want to upgrade the brakes ...<P>so I was wondering if it would be a wise move to change my 86 GT for a 88 GT 5speed ??<P>- The brakes are better (assuming here that they don't need upgrading)<BR>- The suspension is better / more stable (should be a lot less expensive to 'upgrade')<BR>- it would already have the transmission I want <BR>...<P>so what do you Fiero experts think ?<BR>should I stick w. the autom. 86GT & try to upgrade it to a 'modified 88' level or should I get an 88 & upgrade it ??<P>Thanks for your time<BR>Philippe||||reg||1
Z||000001||DJRice||05-08-2001||07:16 PM||||You need to find yourself a properly equipped 1988 V6 5spd.  <P>While swapping the transmission is certainly possible, I would have to give that 5 out of 5 stars on the PITA scale.  Given the fact that the hydraulic clutches can be tricky to troubleshoot and/or service in cars that rolled off the assembly line with them, if you kinked one line and affected the fluid flow thru the system or did not install the pedal straight, you will get a world of clutch problems that might be very hard to diagnose.<P>The 88s did have a more capable braking system and upgraded suspension, but keep in mind that the 88s are now 13 years old.  If you are that interested in suspension, you are going to want to upgrade some of the suspension parts and the thing may or may not need a brake job.<P>By the time you buy all those parts from a less fortunate 88 car and then dismantle your car to replace them, you will have spent enough time under the car to warrant buying an 88 outright and selling the 86.  <P>Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kwez||05-08-2001||08:55 PM||||ok, cool.<BR>That clutch thing is a good enough reason to find an 88 5speed !<P>There's a 88 GT 5speed for sale here around Montreal for $8000CAD (86 GTs go for about $5000) I should have a look at it. Let's hope I can sale mine 1st !<P>Jay, what do you think the prices should be like for a 88GT stick ? Anything nice available in "your part of Canada" ?<BR>(sorry, but I can't afford $18000 right now ;-)<P>||||reg||1
